{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 bore carries a tight ISO fit tolerance of 0.018 mm, but the drawing does not account for the thickness added by the I.Z.B.P. plating; after plating the hole will be undersize and the mating shaft may not assemble. The designer should either increase the pre-plate bore size to allow for coating build-up or add a note requiring the bore to be masked or re-machined after plating."

    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Increase the pre-plate bore size to allow for coating build-up or add a note requiring the bore to be masked or re-machined after plating."}]}
